    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If a jogger starts ahead, the train must first erase the gap and then move enough to get its full length past the jogger.\n\nSuppose the train is 120 m long and its front is 180 m behind the jogger. To pass completely, relative gain needed = 180 + 120 = 300 m.",
