    "teach_6": {
      "id": "teach_6",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A cyclist is almost a point, but some questions give the cycle a length. Then add that length too.\n\nA 199 m train passing a 1 m cycle covers 200 m relative to the cyclist. At train speed 15 m/s and cyclist speed 5 m/s in the same direction, relative speed is 10 m/s, so time is 20 s.",
