    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Two overtaking times can reveal both train speed and length. Let train speed be v m/s and length L.\n\nPassing a 3 m/s walker in 12 s gives L = 12(v − 3).\nPassing a 5 m/s walker in 15 s gives L = 15(v − 5).",
